feat(pairing): Bluetooth-style pairing between instances on the tailnet

Owner side (apps/api): POST /pairing/start (auth'd) mints a 4-digit code,
single live session, 2-min TTL, 5-attempt budget; POST /pairing/claim is
open by design (the joiner has no token yet) and trades the code for the
API token. Stale codes from ended sessions read as no_pairing_in_progress
and never burn the live session's budget. /health now reports an instance
name for the discovery list.

Client side (apps/desktop/electron/discovery.ts): tailscale status --json
peers probed for a Kotys daemon; claim via /pairing/claim. New IPC
backend:discover / backend:pair with strict request guards (dotted-quad
host, exactly-4-digit code).

UI: PairingPanel in Settings > Backend (scan, pick instance, enter the
code its panel shows, pair and restart). Paste-code flow stays as
fallback.